<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">22 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 22 November, from 845 to 1975.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/nominoe" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nominoe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">845 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,181 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nominoe's Bretons defeat Charles the Bald at Ballon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Breton ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nominoe">Nominoe</a> defeated the West Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a> at Ballon, near Bains-sur-Oust in eastern Brittany. Charles was forced to accept Nominoe's authority in Brittany, a key step towards an independent Breton kingdom.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ballon">Battle of Ballon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1210">1210 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">816 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Simon de Montfort takes the castle of Termes</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a siege of nearly four months in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albigensian-crusade">Albigensian Crusade</a>, the castle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiermes">Termes</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/languedoc">Languedoc</a> fell to Simon de Montfort, in the crusaders' effort to eliminate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catharism">Catharism</a>, a Christian sect regarded as heretical, from southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albigensian-crusade">Albigensian Crusade</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-de-montfort-5th-earl-of-leicester">Simon de Montfort</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1220">1220 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">806 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Frederick II is crowned Holy Roman Emperor in Rome</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-honorius-iii">Pope Honorius III</a> crowned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a> emperor in St Peter's. Brilliant and controversial, the 'wonder of the world' ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> and spent much of his reign in conflict with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honorius">Honorius</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1307">1307 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">719 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Clement V orders the arrest of all Knights Templar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the bull Pastoralis praeeminentiae, Pope Clement V ordered all Christian monarchs to arrest the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-templar">Knights Templar</a> and seize their property. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-iv-of-france">Philip IV of France</a>, who owed the Templars a great deal of money, had begun the arrests in October.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-templar">Knights Templar</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1497">1497 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">529 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Vasco da Gama rounds the Cape of Good Hope</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasco-da-gama">Vasco da Gama</a>'s Portuguese fleet rounded the southern tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> on its way to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. The voyage opened a direct sea route from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> and the rise of a Portuguese trading empire.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-of-good-hope">Cape of Good Hope</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasco-da-gama">Vasco da Gama</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1635">1635 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">391 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Dutch East India Company begins its pacification campaign on Taiwan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a>, which held little of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> beyond its fortress at Tayouan, launched a campaign to subdue hostile aboriginal villages in the island's south-west. It brought the middle and south of the island under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> control.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1963">1963 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">President Kennedy is assassinated in Dallas</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">John F. Kennedy was shot dead while riding in an open motorcade through Dealey Plaza in Dallas. Vice-President Lyndon Johnson was sworn in aboard Air Force One the same afternoon.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1975">1975 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">51 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Juan Carlos is proclaimed king of Spain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Two days after Franco's death, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-carlos-i">Juan Carlos de Borbón</a> was proclaimed king. Expected to preserve the dictatorship, he instead guided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>'s transition to a parliamentary democracy.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 22 November <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mary-of-guise"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mary-of-guise.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mary of Guise</span><span class="tp">1515–1560</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-ii-deste"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alfonso-ii-deste.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alfonso II d'Este</span><span class="tp">1533–1597</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pierre-de-rigaud-marquis-de-vaudreuil-cavagnial"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pierre-de-rigaud-marquis-de-vaudreuil-cavagnial.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pierre de Rigaud, Marquis de Vaudreuil-Cavagnial</span><span class="tp">1698–1778</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-frederick-grand-duke-of-baden"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-frederick-grand-duke-of-baden.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles Frederick, Grand Duke of Baden</span><span class="tp">1728–1811</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-eliot"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-eliot.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George Eliot</span><span class="tp">1819–1880</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ranavalona-iii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ranavalona-iii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ranavalona III</span><span class="tp">1861–1917</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/enver-pasha"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/enver-pasha.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Enver Pasha</span><span class="tp">1881–1922</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/philippe-leclerc-de-hauteclocque"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/philippe-leclerc-de-hauteclocque.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Philippe Leclerc de Hauteclocque</span><span class="tp">1902–1947</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 22 November <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lothair-ii-of-italy"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lothair-ii-of-italy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lothair II of Italy</span><span class="tp">c. 926–950</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/as-salih-ayyub"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/as-salih-ayyub.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">As-Salih Ayyub</span><span class="tp">1205–1249</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/blackbeard"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/blackbeard.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Blackbeard</span><span class="tp">c. 1680–1718</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/robert-clive"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/robert-clive.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Robert Clive</span><span class="tp">1725–1774</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/walter-reed"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/walter-reed.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Walter Reed</span><span class="tp">1851–1902</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-f-kennedy"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">John F. Kennedy</span><span class="tp">1917–1963</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
